   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <opener>
                        <dateline>
                            <date when="1920-07-04">4/7/20</date> <name type="geo" key="G_ITA_VENI">Venezia</name>
                        </dateline>
                    </opener>
                    <p>Grazie della cartolina. Andiamo tutti a <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI">Parigi</name> per un mese. Mi scriva <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI_40">Hotel de l’Elysée, 9, rue de Beaune, Paris</name>. Le manderò presto la traduzione italiana della <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">mia <rs type="work" key="W_EXILES">commedia</rs>
                        </seg> con una dedica.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>Una stretta di mano.</salute>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                        <signed hand="#barn84">
                            <name type="person" key="barn84">Nora Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                        <signed hand="#joyc07">
                            <name type="person" key="joyc07">Lucia</name>
                        </signed>
                        <signed hand="#joyc05">
                            <name type="person" key="joyc05">Giorgio</name>
                        </signed>
                    </closer>
                </div>
                <div type="translation">
                    <opener>
                        <dateline>
                            <date when="1920-07-04">4/7/20</date> <name type="geo" key="G_ITA_VENI">Venice</name>
                        </dateline>
                    </opener>
                    <p>Thank you for the card. We are all going to Paris for a month. Write to me at Hotel de l’Elysée, 9, rue de Beaune, Paris. I’ll soon send you the Italian translation of my comedy with a dedication.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>A handshake.</salute>
                        <signed>James Joyce</signed>
                        <signed>Nora Joyce</signed>
                        <signed>Lucia</signed>
                        <signed>Giorgio</signed>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div> <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="global-note1" type="global">The image is “VENEZIA – Canal grande”. This watercolor may be by Gian Luciano Sormani, but it appears to lack his distinctive scrawled signature, or perhaps that was omitted from the card.</note>
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">The Italian translation of JJ’s play <name type="work" key="W_EXILES">Exiles</name>, “Esuli”, was published in <hi rend="italic">Il Convegno</hi> 1, no. 3 (April 1920): 28-52; no. 4 (May 1920): 27-46; no. 5 (June 1920): 22-37.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
   </text>
